`f

CORE is an informal community for anyone enthusiastic or curious about radio — whether you're new to radio and want to learn or you've been tinkering for years and want to share. Ham radio operators, GMRS users, Meshtastic fans, software-defined radio nerds, makers, and technical and non-technical folks are all welcome. No experience required or expected.

`[ Read more about CORE`:/page/about.mu]

>`BT2b1c0e`FTff6e00Next Meeting

`FTff6e00`!Tuesday, October 6, 2026`!`f

`!Open Source Radio Projects: Hammunition, Skid Finder, and SolarStorm Scout`!
`FT9a7040Moshe "ChiefGyk3D"`f

`FTc8a06a`! When`!`f        6:00–9:00 PM
`FTc8a06a`! Where`!`f       CGI, 570 Polaris Pkwy, Suite 200, Westerville, Ohio 43082
`FTc8a06a`! Finding Us`!`f  Second floor, at the end of the hallway
`FTc8a06a`! RSVP`!`f        `[tally.so/r/2E04Vj`https://tally.so/r/2E04Vj]

Join Moshe for a hands-on showcase of several open-source projects he's actively developing around amateur radio, RF experimentation, Linux, and field use. He'll demo Hammunition, a Linux-based radio software suite; Hammunition Hill, its companion dashboard; Skid Finder, a Bluetooth-based signal tracking and foxhunting toolkit; and SolarStorm Scout, a space-weather monitoring and alerting project.

These projects are still in active alpha and beta development, so this isn't just a presentation. It's an open call for fellow radio enthusiasts to test the software, break things, report bugs, suggest features, and provide real-world feedback to help shape where these projects go next.

`FTc8a06a`!Project repos`!`f
`[ Hammunition`https://github.com/ChiefGyk3D/Hammunition]   `[ Hammunition Hill`https://github.com/ChiefGyk3D/hammunition-hill]
`[ Skid Finder`https://github.com/ChiefGyk3D/Skid-Finder]   `[ SolarStorm Scout`https://github.com/ChiefGyk3D/solarstorm_scout]

>`BT2b1c0e`FTff6e00Meetings

We get together the first Tuesday of every month. Doors open at 6 PM and talks start at 6:30. The location may vary, but we're normally at CGI in Westerville. Bring nothing but yourself and some curiosity — and a project or gadget if you've got one.

Meetings are casual gatherings where you can listen to a talk, see and share projects, and chat with other radio curious folks. Maybe you'll even want to give a talk yourself! And, of course, a trip to the pub afterwards is always on the table.

`[ Upcoming Meetings`:/page/meetings.mu]   `[ Past Meetings`:/page/past-meetings.mu]

>`BT2b1c0e`FTff6e00Get Involved

`!Discord`! is the heart of CORE. That's where we coordinate meetups, share projects, ask questions, and get to know each other between first Tuesdays. If you want to reach out directly — to give a talk, help organize, or just ask something — message the admins there.

You can also connect `!on the air`!. We call out on 147.555 MHz simplex, we've got a Meshtastic channel you can scan your way onto, and we run a Reticulum gateway at rns.core.radio that you can reach over the Internet. Or you can set up a Reticulum node over LoRa.

Like to code? We're on `!GitHub`! as well. The code and materials from past talks, whatever projects people are collaborating on, and this website are all available there.

Prefer email? You can get meeting announcements in your inbox. Sign up for the `!mailing list`! by mailing core-dot-radio+subscribe@googlegroups.com. We won't spam you and you can unsubscribe at any time. And you can email us directly at hello@core.radio.

